{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The claim needs a country, year, and definition of income to be assessed accurately. “Average income” could mean individual earnings, household income, or income per person, and “average” could mean the mean or median.\n\n**If you mean the United States, the claim is generally false:** standard national statistics show Black Americans’ median household income below the national median. Mean income and individual earnings are different measures and should be checked separately.\n\nAn average for a group also tells you little about any particular person’s income."}}
